{"zh":[{"start":0.0,"end":2.19,"text":"飓风哈维、艾尔玛和玛丽亚"},{"start":2.21,"end":4.3,"text":"登陆时造成了巨大破坏。"},{"start":4.32,"end":7.12,"text":"它们都被列为强飓风，"},{"start":7.14,"end":12.3,"text":"但它们之所以这么危险，部分原因是它们在登陆前迅速增强。"},{"start":12.32,"end":16.21,"text":"当飓风在短时间内大幅增强时，"},{"start":16.23,"end":19.29,"text":"科学家把这个过程叫做快速增强。"},{"start":19.31,"end":24.5,"text":"这是风暴最难预报的方面，也可能对人们的生命最为关键。"},{"start":24.52,"end":27.89,"text":"虽然任何飓风都可能威胁生命、造成破坏——"},{"start":27.91,"end":30.74,"text":"风暴潮、洪水和极端大风，"},{"start":30.76,"end":34.81,"text":"但快速增强的飓风会大大增加这些风险，"},{"start":34.83,"end":38.57,"text":"同时留给人们准备和撤离的时间很有限。"},{"start":38.59,"end":43.03,"text":"快速增强指的是飓风的最大持续风速"},{"start":43.05,"end":49.28,"text":"在 24 小时内至少增加每小时 35 英里，往往会形成强飓风。"},{"start":49.3,"end":53.53,"text":"最近一次快速增强的大西洋风暴是飓风玛丽亚，"},{"start":53.55,"end":58.86,"text":"它在不到 18 小时内从 1 级发展成 5 级飓风。"},{"start":58.88,"end":63.56,"text":"过去几十年里，追踪飓风路径的预报误差已经减小。"},{"start":63.58,"end":67.44,"text":"强度预报的误差最近虽然有所改善，"},{"start":67.46,"end":71.85,"text":"但因为快速增强的风暴，仍可能出现很大的误差。"},{"start":71.87,"end":78.09,"text":"不过，从 NASA 卫星上能看到飓风快速增强的线索。"},{"start":78.11,"end":82.58,"text":"科学家说，海水必须够暖——华氏 80 度或更高。"},{"start":82.6,"end":85.13,"text":"还需要较小的垂直风切变，"},{"start":85.15,"end":87.78,"text":"也就是风随高度变化不大，"},{"start":87.8,"end":91.84,"text":"这样风暴的中心部分才不会被吹歪或撕裂。"},{"start":91.86,"end":95.53,"text":"可能快速增强的风暴，一个关键指标"},{"start":95.55,"end":99.41,"text":"是风眼周围有一圈对称而深厚的降水带。"},{"start":99.43,"end":104.3,"text":"快速增强的风暴通常一个飓风季最多出现两次。"},{"start":104.32,"end":108.35,"text":"但 2017 年，我们看到了四场风暴快速增强，"},{"start":108.37,"end":112.91,"text":"科学家把原因归于更暖的海水和有利的风。"},{"start":112.93,"end":116.66,"text":"但这些关键因素并不总会导致快速增强"},{"start":116.68,"end":119.09,"text":"——说明这是个复杂得多的问题。"},{"start":119.11,"end":125.46,"text":"研究人员说，有许多小尺度过程，比如和强雷暴有关的过程，"},{"start":125.48,"end":128.57,"text":"会影响飓风变得多强。"},{"start":128.59,"end":131.78,"text":"像 NASA 全球降水观测任务这样的卫星"},{"start":131.8,"end":135.14,"text":"能观测到发展中的风暴内部的降水，"},{"start":135.16,"end":141.28,"text":"帮助科学家更好地理解这些过程怎样共同作用，使飓风增强。"}],"de":[],"en":[{"start":0.0,"end":2.19,"text":"Hurricane Harvey, Irma, and Maria","words":[["Hurricane","飓风"],["Harvey,","哈维"],["Irma,","艾尔玛"],["and","和"],["Maria","玛丽亚"]]},{"start":2.21,"end":4.3,"text":"wreaked havoc when they made landfall.","words":[["wreaked","造成"],["havoc","破坏"],["when","当"],["they","它们"],["made","做"],["landfall.","登陆"]]},{"start":4.32,"end":7.12,"text":"They were all categorized as major hurricanes,","words":[["They","它们"],["were","曾"],["all","都"],["categorized","被归类"],["as","作为"],["major","强"],["hurricanes,","飓风"]]},{"start":7.14,"end":12.3,"text":"but part of what made them so dangerous was how they rapidly intensified before moving inland.","words":[["but","但"],["part","部分"],["of","的"],["what","什么"],["made","使"],["them","它们"],["so","如此"],["dangerous","危险"],["was","曾是"],["how","怎样"],["they","它们"],["rapidly","迅速"],["intensified","增强"],["before","在…前"],["moving","移动"],["inland.","内陆"]]},{"start":12.32,"end":16.21,"text":"When hurricanes intensify a large amount in a short period,","words":[["When","当"],["hurricanes","飓风"],["intensify","增强"],["a","一个"],["large","大"],["amount","量"],["in","在"],["a","一个"],["short","短"],["period,","时期"]]},{"start":16.23,"end":19.29,"text":"scientists call this process rapid intensification.","words":[["scientists","科学家"],["call","称"],["this","这个"],["process","过程"],["rapid","快速"],["intensification.","增强"]]},{"start":19.31,"end":24.5,"text":"This is the hardest aspect of a storm to forecast and it can be most critical to people’s lives.","words":[["This","这"],["is","是"],["the","这"],["hardest","最难"],["aspect","方面"],["of","的"],["a","一场"],["storm","风暴"],["to","去"],["forecast","预报"],["and","而"],["it","它"],["can","能"],["be","是"],["most","最"],["critical","关键"],["to","对"],["people’s","人们的"],["lives.","生命"]]},{"start":24.52,"end":27.89,"text":"While any hurricane can threaten lives and cause damage","words":[["While","虽然"],["any","任何"],["hurricane","飓风"],["can","能"],["threaten","威胁"],["lives","生命"],["and","和"],["cause","造成"],["damage","破坏"]]},{"start":27.91,"end":30.74,"text":"with storm surges, floods, and extreme winds,","words":[["with","以"],["storm","风暴"],["surges,","潮"],["floods,","洪水"],["and","和"],["extreme","极端"],["winds,","风"]]},{"start":30.76,"end":34.81,"text":"a rapidly intensifying hurricane can greatly increase these risks","words":[["a","一个"],["rapidly","快速"],["intensifying","增强的"],["hurricane","飓风"],["can","能"],["greatly","大大"],["increase","增加"],["these","这些"],["risks","风险"]]},{"start":34.83,"end":38.57,"text":"while giving populations limited time to prepare and evacuate.","words":[["while","同时"],["giving","给"],["populations","人群"],["limited","有限的"],["time","时间"],["to","去"],["prepare","准备"],["and","和"],["evacuate.","撤离"]]},{"start":38.59,"end":43.03,"text":"Rapid intensification occurs when a hurricane’s maximum sustained winds","words":[["Rapid","快速"],["intensification","增强"],["occurs","发生"],["when","当"],["a","一个"],["hurricane’s","飓风的"],["maximum","最大"],["sustained","持续"],["winds","风速"]]},{"start":43.05,"end":49.28,"text":"increase at least 35 miles per hour in 24 hours and often results in major hurricanes.","words":[["increase","增加"],["at","至少"],["least",""],["35","35"],["miles","英里"],["per","每"],["hour","小时"],["in","在"],["24","24"],["hours","小时"],["and","和"],["often","常常"],["results","导致"],["in","在"],["major","强"],["hurricanes.","飓风"]]},{"start":49.3,"end":53.53,"text":"The latest Atlantic storm to rapidly intensify was Hurricane Maria,","words":[["The","这"],["latest","最近"],["Atlantic","大西洋"],["storm","风暴"],["to","去"],["rapidly","快速"],["intensify","增强"],["was","曾是"],["Hurricane","飓风"],["Maria,","玛丽亚"]]},{"start":53.55,"end":58.86,"text":"which developed from a Category 1 to a Category 5 hurricane in less than 18 hours.","words":[["which","它"],["developed","发展"],["from","从"],["a","一个"],["Category","级别"],["1","1"],["to","到"],["a","一个"],["Category","级别"],["5","5"],["hurricane","飓风"],["in","在"],["less","不到"],["than","于"],["18","18"],["hours.","小时"]]},{"start":58.88,"end":63.56,"text":"In the past few decades, forecasting errors for tracking hurricanes have decreased.","words":[["In","在"],["the","这"],["past","过去"],["few","几"],["decades,","十年"],["forecasting","预报"],["errors","误差"],["for","为"],["tracking","追踪"],["hurricanes","飓风"],["have","已"],["decreased.","减小"]]},{"start":63.58,"end":67.44,"text":"While intensity forecast errors have shown recent improvement,","words":[["While","虽然"],["intensity","强度"],["forecast","预报"],["errors","误差"],["have","已"],["shown","显示"],["recent","最近"],["improvement,","改善"]]},{"start":67.46,"end":71.85,"text":"significant errors can still occur because of rapidly intensifying storms.","words":[["significant","显著的"],["errors","误差"],["can","能"],["still","仍"],["occur","发生"],["because","因为"],["of","于"],["rapidly","快速"],["intensifying","增强的"],["storms.","风暴"]]},{"start":71.87,"end":78.09,"text":"There are, however, clues to a rapidly intensifying hurricane that can be seen from NASA satellites.","words":[["There","有"],["are,","是"],["however,","然而"],["clues","线索"],["to","对"],["a","一个"],["rapidly","快速"],["intensifying","增强的"],["hurricane","飓风"],["that","那"],["can","能"],["be","被"],["seen","看到"],["from","从"],["NASA","NASA"],["satellites.","卫星"]]},{"start":78.11,"end":82.58,"text":"Scientists say ocean water needs to be warm - 80 Degrees Fahrenheit or higher.","words":[["Scientists","科学家"],["say","说"],["ocean","海洋"],["water","水"],["needs","需要"],["to",""],["be","是"],["warm","暖"],["-","-"],["80","80"],["Degrees","度"],["Fahrenheit","华氏"],["or","或"],["higher.","更高"]]},{"start":82.6,"end":85.13,"text":"There also needs to be low vertical wind shear,","words":[["There","有"],["also","也"],["needs","需要"],["to",""],["be","是"],["low","低"],["vertical","垂直"],["wind","风"],["shear,","切变"]]},{"start":85.15,"end":87.78,"text":"meaning winds that don’t change much with altitude,","words":[["meaning","意思是"],["winds","风"],["that","那"],["don’t","不"],["change","变化"],["much","很多"],["with","随"],["altitude,","高度"]]},{"start":87.8,"end":91.84,"text":"so that the central part of the storm doesn’t get tilted over or ripped apart.","words":[["so","以便"],["that","那"],["the","这"],["central","中心"],["part","部分"],["of","的"],["the","这"],["storm","风暴"],["doesn’t","不"],["get","被"],["tilted","倾斜"],["over","歪"],["or","或"],["ripped","撕"],["apart.","裂"]]},{"start":91.86,"end":95.53,"text":"A key indicator of a potentially rapidly intensifying storm","words":[["A","一个"],["key","关键"],["indicator","指标"],["of","的"],["a","一个"],["potentially","可能"],["rapidly","快速"],["intensifying","增强的"],["storm","风暴"]]},{"start":95.55,"end":99.41,"text":"storm is a symmetrical, deep ring of precipitation surrounding the eye.","words":[["storm","风暴"],["is","是"],["a","一个"],["symmetrical,","对称的"],["deep","深厚的"],["ring","环"],["of","的"],["precipitation","降水"],["surrounding","围绕"],["the","这"],["eye.","风眼"]]},{"start":99.43,"end":104.3,"text":"Rapidly intensifying storms typically occur up to twice in a hurricane season.","words":[["Rapidly","快速"],["intensifying","增强的"],["storms","风暴"],["typically","通常"],["occur","发生"],["up","达"],["to","至"],["twice","两次"],["in","在"],["a","一个"],["hurricane","飓风"],["season.","季"]]},{"start":104.32,"end":108.35,"text":"But in 2017, we have seen four storms rapidly intensify","words":[["But","但"],["in","在"],["2017,","2017年"],["we","我们"],["have","已"],["seen","看到"],["four","四场"],["storms","风暴"],["rapidly","快速"],["intensify","增强"]]},{"start":108.37,"end":112.91,"text":"and scientists attribute this to warmer ocean waters and favorable winds.","words":[["and","和"],["scientists","科学家"],["attribute","归因"],["this","这"],["to","于"],["warmer","更暖的"],["ocean","海洋"],["waters","水"],["and","和"],["favorable","有利的"],["winds.","风"]]},{"start":112.93,"end":116.66,"text":"But these key ingredients don’t always lead to rapid intensification","words":[["But","但"],["these","这些"],["key","关键"],["ingredients","因素"],["don’t","不"],["always","总是"],["lead","导致"],["to","到"],["rapid","快速"],["intensification","增强"]]},{"start":116.68,"end":119.09,"text":"-- proving that it’s a much more complex problem.","words":[["--","—"],["proving","证明"],["that","那"],["it’s","它是"],["a","一个"],["much","很"],["more","更"],["complex","复杂的"],["problem.","问题"]]},{"start":119.11,"end":125.46,"text":"Researchers say there are many small-scale processes, such as those associated with deep thunderstorms,","words":[["Researchers","研究人员"],["say","说"],["there","有"],["are","是"],["many","许多"],["small-scale","小尺度"],["processes,","过程"],["such","比如"],["as","如"],["those","那些"],["associated","相关"],["with","与"],["deep","强"],["thunderstorms,","雷暴"]]},{"start":125.48,"end":128.57,"text":"that influence how strong a hurricane becomes.","words":[["that","那"],["influence","影响"],["how","多"],["strong","强"],["a","一个"],["hurricane","飓风"],["becomes.","变得"]]},{"start":128.59,"end":131.78,"text":"Satellites such as NASA’s Global Precipitation Measurement Mission","words":[["Satellites","卫星"],["such","比如"],["as","如"],["NASA’s","NASA的"],["Global","全球"],["Precipitation","降水"],["Measurement","观测"],["Mission","任务"]]},{"start":131.8,"end":135.14,"text":"can observe precipitation inside evolving storms","words":[["can","能"],["observe","观测"],["precipitation","降水"],["inside","在里面"],["evolving","发展中的"],["storms","风暴"]]},{"start":135.16,"end":141.28,"text":"and help scientists better understand how these processes come together to intensify hurricanes.","words":[["and","和"],["help","帮助"],["scientists","科学家"],["better","更好"],["understand","理解"],["how","如何"],["these","这些"],["processes","过程"],["come","来"],["together","一起"],["to","去"],["intensify","增强"],["hurricanes.","飓风"]]}]}